---
description: Prevent accidental file deletion or reorganization by the agent
alwaysApply: true
---

# No Delete Without Approval

- Never run `rm`, `git rm`, `git clean`, or delete/move/rename files unless the user explicitly requests it in the current message.
- Never move tracked files without `git mv`.
- Before any cleanup that touches more than one file, run `git ls-files --deleted` and stop if non-empty.
- Prefer `git restore` over deletion when fixing drift.
- Never edit paths listed in `.cursorignore`.
- If a file must be removed from git tracking, use `git rm --cached` only with explicit user approval.
